  "distanceMi": 3.8,
  "priceTier": 1,
  "bangPlus": false,
  "opensAt": "11:30 AM",
  "closesAt": "9:20 PM",
  "address": "1140 Pinewreath Crossing Plaza, Unit D-6 (behind the nail salon, share the lot with the tax place), Loam Springs",
  "about": "We opened in 2017 after our old counter on Kessel Road lost its lease. My sister Amy does the snow bowls and I do the tea, and we are both here every day, which is why it sometimes takes a minute. Everything is shaken to order.",
  "announcement": "THE SEALING MACHINE IS FIXED. Sorry to everybody last week, we were sending drinks out with press lids and they leaked in the bags. Also we can not do half sugar on the snow bowls anymore because it comes out seperate. If something is wrong with your order please call the shop at (555) 0142 before you rate us and we will remake it. - Teresa",
  "promos": [
   {
    "text": "FREE CAN OF SODA WITH ORDERS OVER $40",
    "kind": "none"
   }
  ],
  "reviews": [
   {
    "name": "Priya N.",
    "stars": 5,
    "date": "Aug 16",
    "text": "I have been coming here since the Kessel Road shop and I want to say that the brown sugar pearls are still cooked fresh, which nobody else in this town does anymore. Teresa remembers that I take 25% sugar and she starts it before I finish saying it. The delivery took an hour and eleven minutes and I would do it again."
   },
   {
    "name": "Dale W.",
    "stars": 1,
    "date": "Aug 11",
    "text": "Lot is impossible. The tax place takes every space and there is a truck that parks across two of them all afternoon. Never got a drink."
   },
   {
    "name": "Marisol C.",
    "stars": 5,
    "date": "Aug 04",
    "text": "Ordered the mango snow in Sharing and it arrived as an intact mountain. My kids ate around it for forty minutes. The condensed milk is charged separately and honestly that is fine."
   },
   {
    "name": "Kenji A.",
    "stars": 4,
    "date": "Jul 29",
    "text": "Good tea. I selected No Ice and was billed for displaced volume, which was explained to me on the receipt in a way I did not expect from a bubble tea shop."
   },
   {
    "name": "Brandi S.",
    "stars": 2,
    "date": "Jul 19",
    "text": "Called about a catering order and the phone rang for a long time. Someone finally picked up and said they were both making drinks. I understand it but I still had to go to the other place."
   },
   {
    "name": "Officer T. Rowe",
    "stars": 5,
    "date": "Jul 02",
    "text": "The black sesame is not sweet and the menu says so in capital letters. I read it, I ordered it, I liked it. Everyone complaining did not read it."
   }
  ],
